<section class="section" aria-labelledby="start-title">
  <div class="wrap two-col">
    <div>
      <h2 id="start-title">The only official site</h2>
      <p class="udyam-url">{% ext "https://udyamregistration.gov.in/", "udyamregistration.gov.in" %}</p>
      <p>The portal says: "This is the only Government Portal for MSME (Udyam) Registration" and warns visitors to "Beware of Fake Sites."</p>
      <h3 class="udyam-h3">How to spot a lookalike</h3>
      <ul class="tick-list tick-list--no plain-list">
        <li>The address does not end in <strong>.gov.in</strong></li>
        <li>It asks for a "government fee" or "registration charge"</li>
        <li>It appears at the top of search results as an advertisement</li>
        <li>It uses "official", "Udyam" or an emblem in its branding, with a small note that it is private</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
    <div>
      <h2>Current limits</h2>
      <p>As published on the Udyam portal, for the definition applying from 1 April 2025. Both limits must be met.</p>
      <section class="data-table-wrap" tabindex="0" aria-label="MSME limits, scrolls sideways on small screens">
        <table class="data-table table-narrow">
          <thead><tr><th scope="col">Type</th><th scope="col">Investment up to</th><th scope="col">Turnover up to</th></tr></thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr><th scope="row">Micro</th><td>₹2.5 crore</td><td>₹10 crore</td></tr>
            <tr><th scope="row">Small</th><td>₹25 crore</td><td>₹100 crore</td></tr>
            <tr><th scope="row">Medium</th><td>₹125 crore</td><td>₹500 crore</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </section>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section section--tint" aria-labelledby="paid-title">
  <div class="wrap two-col">
    <div>
      <h2 id="paid-title">When paying for help can make sense</h2>
      <p>Assistance is optional, and any fee is for a private person's time. It is not a government charge. It may be worth considering if:</p>
      <ul class="tick-list plain-list">
        <li>You have an old registration, or errors to correct</li>
        <li>You are unsure how your investment and turnover should be worked out</li>
        <li>You are unsure which activity code fits your business</li>
        <li>You have a group of related businesses</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
    <div>
      <h2>If you do pay someone</h2>
      <ul class="tick-list plain-list">
        <li>Ask them to confirm in writing that the fee is theirs and not the government's</li>
        <li>Stay with them while they use your details, or do it yourself with their guidance</li>
        <li>Use your own mobile number and email</li>
        <li>Check the result on the official portal</li>
        <li>Be wary of paid "renewal" offers. The portal does not ask for fees</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section" aria-labelledby="after-title">
  <div class="wrap prose">
    <h2 id="after-title" class="first-h2">What registration does and does not do</h2>
    <p>Udyam registration records your business as an MSME and is often asked for when seeking MSME-related schemes or support. It does not by itself secure a loan, subsidy or tender, and it is a different thing from {% routeLink "/services/gst-registration/", "GST registration" %} or {% routeLink "/services/company-llp-registration/", "forming a company" %}.</p>
    <p>Check the benefit you are interested in against the relevant scheme's own rules. We have not reviewed individual schemes here.</p>
    <p>Reading this page is all many people need. If you want help with a related accounting question, you can <a href="/request-an-accountant/">describe it to AccountOrbit</a>.</p>
